    "criterion_literal": "Corregir solo el kill guard debe llevar N_pe/end de 82,304 a un valor\nentre 200 y 600. Por encima de 600 sin haber tocado el reflector, el\nmodelo del acoplamiento entre defectos es incorrecto y debe reportarse\ncomo tal. Por debajo de 200, la corrección no explica el déficit y hay\nun tercer defecto sin identificar.\n\ngKilledWorld debe caer aproximadamente a 1,18 millones (los\nFresnelRefraction más residuos), y gSparedWorldReflection debe quedar\ndel orden de 3,9 millones. Desviaciones grandes en cualquiera de los\ndos indican que el status leído no corresponde a la frontera.\n\nEl residual del balance de fotones debe mantenerse por debajo del 10 %.",
    "counter_definitions": "gKilledWorld and gSparedWorldReflection count guard actions/visits, not deduplicated photons; a surviving photon can revisit the guard. Spared events are not a terminal loss. Current-step boundary status is snapshotted only for optical fGeomBoundary; other steps keep Undefined and the original kill behavior.",
    "yield_definition": "END mean=(END_L+END_R)/(2*N_generated_events), including zeros; uncertainty is event-level sample SEM. TOP is total detected hits summed over all 500 events.",
    "balance_definition": "Operational observable ledger: generated_scintillation minus detected_SiPM_TTree_hits minus all OpBoundary Absorption statuses minus gKilledWorld. Retain signed residual and residual/N_scint. Do not count reflection, StepTooSmall, or refraction into wrap as a terminal sink. Bulk absorption, wavelength/null-world kills and creator-specific attribution are not stored by the existing schema; mark these UNVERIFIED, not zero. Counts include optical populations while generation counter is scintillation-only, so a strictly disjoint scintillation-track conservation balance cannot be certified. Report this limitation with the measured ledger rather than invent missing losses.",
    "scope": "One correction commit with the inseparable spare counter only. No other physics edit, rerun-to-target, reflector A/B or new unapproved telemetry."
  },
